+`rnnt_joint_batch_frames` changes the number of encoder frames evaluated by one
+speculative RNNT joint call, not the amount of audio decoded or the number of
+tokens emitted. Positive values reduce work discarded after an emission; a
+blank-only batch advances to the next batch with the predictor cache intact.
+Smaller batches can add graph-call overhead, so measure the tradeoff for the
+selected backend and workload. The default `0` retains unrestricted lookahead;
+negative values are invalid. CTC and TDT decoding do not use this setting.
+
